    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the business-day rule in `BusinessDay.java` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BusinessDay.java`) so the registration date rolls past public holidays in addition to weekends.\n\n**What changed:**\n- Added the fixed public-holiday calendar as a `Set<LocalDate>`: 2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28.\n- Rewrote `rollForward` to loop, advancing one day at a time until it reaches a date that is neither a Saturday/Sunday nor a listed holiday. This naturally handles chains \u2014 e.g. Fri 2026-12-25 (holiday) \u2192 Sat/Sun \u2192 Mon 2026-12-28 (holiday) \u2192 Tue 2026-12-29 (business day).\n\nThe single public method contract required by the OfficeFloor wiring is preserved, and the callers (`BuildOwner`, which feeds `AssignMembershipNumber` and `CheckOwnerDailyLimit`) are unchanged since they already consume the adjusted date.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest` and the full suite pass (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS). The acceptance test asserts the invariant that the default registration date is never a weekend, which the holiday-aware roll-forward continues to satisfy.",
